### Local-AI-Doc-Summarizer-API — smoke tests
### Start the API first:  dotnet run --project src/Api
### Ollama must be running and the model pulled:
###   ollama serve
###   ollama pull qwen3:1.7b-q4_K_M
###
### A 1.7B model on CPU-only hardware is slow. Expect MINUTES, not seconds.

@host = http://localhost:5000
@samples = D:/AI Projs/Local-AI-Doc-Summarizer-API/samples

### 1. Health — should be 200 with ollama.reachable = true and modelPresent = true
###    Returns 503 when Ollama is down, so an orchestrator can act on the status code.
GET {{host}}/health
Accept: application/json

### 2. Arabic TXT -> must return an ARABIC summary, not English.
###    This is the key check that language detection is wired end to end.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/summarize/text
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "text": "هذا المستند يشرح عملية تلخيص النصوص باستخدام نماذج لغوية محلية تعمل بالكامل على جهازك. لا تتصل الخدمة بالإنترنت، ولا تغادر بياناتك الجهاز في أي مرحلة من مراحل المعالجة. تعمل الأداة مع ملفات PDF و DOCX و TXT و Markdown، وتكتشف لغة المستند تلقائياً قبل بدء التلخيص. يمكن نشر الخدمة داخل الشبكات المؤسسية دون الحاجة إلى أي اتصال خارجي، مما يجعلها مناسبة للوثائق الحساسة.",
  "language": "auto",
  "maxWords": 80
}

### 3. English text -> English summary. Forces the language instead of detecting it.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/summarize/text
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "text": "The document summarizer runs entirely on the local machine using a small language model served by Ollama. No document content is transmitted to any external service at any stage. The pipeline extracts text, detects the document language, splits the content into overlapping chunks, summarizes each chunk, and merges the partial summaries into a single result. It can be deployed inside corporate networks without internet access, which makes it suitable for confidential documents.",
  "language": "en",
  "maxWords": 80
}

### 4. Force Arabic output from English input — proves the language override works.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/summarize/text
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "text": "This document explains how the local summarization pipeline works and why no data leaves the local machine.",
  "language": "ar",
  "maxWords": 40
}

### 5. Multipart upload — Arabic TXT file. Expect detectedLanguage = "ar".
POST {{host}}/api/v1/summarize
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----smoke

----smoke
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="sample-ar.txt"
Content-Type: text/plain

@{{samples}}/sample-ar.txt
----smoke
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="language"

auto
----smoke
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="maxWords"

80
----smoke--

### 6. Multipart upload — DOCX file, generated by samples/make_pdf.py tooling.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/summarize
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----smoke

----smoke
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="sample.docx"
Content-Type: application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document

@{{samples}}/sample.docx
----smoke
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="maxWords"

60
----smoke--

### 7. Multipart upload — PDF file with a real text layer.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/summarize
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----smoke

----smoke
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="sample.pdf"
Content-Type: application/pdf

@{{samples}}/sample.pdf
----smoke
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="maxWords"

60
----smoke--

### 8. ERROR 422 — unsupported format. Should not reach the model.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/summarize
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----smoke

----smoke
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="notes.rtf"
Content-Type: application/rtf

@{{samples}}/sample-ar.txt
----smoke--

### 9. ERROR 422 — no file part in the request.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/summarize
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----smoke

----smoke
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="language"

auto
----smoke--

### 10. ERROR 400 — body fails validation (empty text, bad language code).
POST {{host}}/api/v1/summarize/text
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "text": "",
  "language": "klingon"
}

### 11. ERROR 502 — stop Ollama first, then run this. Confirms the backend
###     failure path maps to a status code and not an unhandled 500.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/summarize/text
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "text": "If Ollama is not running this request should fail with 502 Bad Gateway rather than crashing the service.",
  "maxWords": 30
}
